From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:25:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ath10k-ct: quiet a pdev param the firmware does not have

ath10k-ct patch 994 (for upstream), B135: on 10.x firmware every radio
start logs "pdev param 0 not supported by firmware" (idle_ps_config,
whose -EOPNOTSUPP ath10k_start() already takes as no error), and every
station association logs it again with "failed to enable peer stats
info: -95" (peer_stats_info_enable, a TLV-firmware param). Report an
unsupported pdev param at debug level, as an unsupported vdev param
is, and let ath10k_bss_assoc() take -EOPNOTSUPP as no error.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/kernel/ath10k-ct/Makefile             |  2 +-
 ...k-ct-quiet-an-unsupported-pdev-param.patch | 52 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/kernel/ath10k-ct/Makefile b/package/kernel/ath10k-ct/Makefile
index 90215eb..5a3a1e1 100644
--- a/package/kernel/ath10k-ct/Makefile
+++ b/package/kernel/ath10k-ct/Makefile
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=ath10k-ct
-PKG_RELEASE:=5
+PKG_RELEASE:=6
 
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPLv2
 PKG_LICENSE_FILES:=
diff --git a/package/kernel/ath10k-ct/patches/994-ath10k-ct-quiet-an-unsupported-pdev-param.patch b/package/kernel/ath10k-ct/patches/994-ath10k-ct-quiet-an-unsupported-pdev-param.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fc0c5c4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/ath10k-ct/patches/994-ath10k-ct-quiet-an-unsupported-pdev-param.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] ath10k-ct: quiet a pdev param the firmware does not have
+
+On 10.x firmware every start of the radio logs
+
+  ath10k_pci 0000:01:00.0: pdev param 0 not supported by firmware
+
+and every association of a station interface logs it again, followed by
+
+  ath10k_pci 0000:01:00.0: failed to enable peer stats info: -95
+
+ath10k_start() sets idle_ps_config and ath10k_bss_assoc() sets
+peer_stats_info_enable, which only the TLV firmware maps; for the others
+the pdev param map holds WMI_PDEV_PARAM_UNSUPPORTED, and the set returns
+-EOPNOTSUPP after a warning. ath10k_start() already takes -EOPNOTSUPP as
+no error, so the warning says nothing.
+
+Report an unsupported pdev param at debug level, as an unsupported vdev
+param already is, and let ath10k_bss_assoc() take -EOPNOTSUPP as no
+error too. A caller that needs the param still warns with the error.
+
+Seen on QCA9882 scan radios (CT 10.1 firmware) on Arista C-260s and a
+W-118: 204 "pdev param 0" and 62 "peer stats info" warnings in 10 hours
+of scans and client tests on one C-260.
+
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/ath10k-7.2/wmi.c
++++ b/ath10k-7.2/wmi.c
+@@ -7288,8 +7288,8 @@ ath10k_wmi_op_gen_pdev_set_param(struct
+ 	struct sk_buff *skb;
+ 
+ 	if (id == WMI_PDEV_PARAM_UNSUPPORTED) {
+-		ath10k_warn(ar, "pdev param %d not supported by firmware\n",
+-			    id);
++		ath10k_dbg(ar, ATH10K_DBG_WMI,
++			   "pdev param %d not supported by firmware\n", id);
+ 		return ERR_PTR(-EOPNOTSUPP);
+ 	}
+ 
+--- a/ath10k-7.2/mac.c
++++ b/ath10k-7.2/mac.c
+@@ -3764,7 +3764,7 @@ static void ath10k_bss_assoc(struct ieee
+ 
+ 	ret = ath10k_wmi_pdev_set_param(ar,
+ 					ar->wmi.pdev_param->peer_stats_info_enable, 1);
+-	if (ret)
++	if (ret && ret != -EOPNOTSUPP)
+ 		ath10k_warn(ar, "failed to enable peer stats info: %d\n", ret);
+ 
+ 	ret = ath10k_wmi_vdev_up(ar, arvif->vdev_id, arvif->aid, arvif->bssid);
-- 
2.52.0
